tip: | Look at the two figures. | The one on the right is not a second drawing. It is the left one flipped, on a linked layer.
tip: 1 | Pose in one color. | A stride reads from the gap between the legs and the arm swung opposite. If the silhouette walks, the rest will.
tip: 3 | Ramps for clothes too. | Jacket, trousers and skin each have a ramp, lit from the left. Three or four steps is plenty at this size.
tip: | Feet on the tile. | The pivot is on the center of a cell, between the feet, so the figure stands in the right place anywhere on a map. Set pivot shows it. | pivot
tip: | Mirror, then update. | Draw one facing only. Update mirror, in the Character section, redoes the flip after an edit. Remember that the light flips too. | pivot
